@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- National Insurance Law, ss 65-68: THE PERIOD THE DEPOSITED TEXT ANSWERS.
--
-- The deposited source is the Law "as amended at retrieval" (2026-10-06). It answers a day
-- only if that text was the text in force on the day. Two pieces of evidence fix the start:
--
-- 1. The amendment tags the consolidation prints on each section. The latest tag on any of
--    ss 65-68 is תשע״ו־3 (on s 68):
-- src:799 | סעיף 65 – פרשנות [תיקון: תשנ״ז, תשס״ט־4]
-- src:813 | סעיף 66 – זכות לקצבת ילדים [תיקון: תשע״ג־3]
-- src:816 | סעיף 67 – מנין ילדים
-- src:820 | סעיף 68 – סכום הקצבה [תיקון: תשס״ב־4, תשס״ב־5, תשס״ב־6, תשס״ג־5, תשס״ג־8, תשס״ג־9, תשס״ג־11, תשס״ג־12, תשס״ד־3, תשס״ד־4, תשס״ד־6, תשס״ו־7, תשס״ט־3, תשע״ג־3, תשע״ו־3]
--    s 1 carries later tags, but its paragraph (2) of "הסכום הבסיסי" reads word for word as
--    the 5776 Law substituted it (below), so no later amendment changed that paragraph.
--    s 1's updating clause did change later (the 2025 freeze), and that clause is not
--    encoded here: the figures it produces are taken as published (nii-il06-published-figures.l4).
--
-- 2. The commencement of the amending Law. Counting the entries of the file's own list of
--    amending Laws (line 7), תשע״ו־3 is the Economic Efficiency Law (Legislative Amendments
--    for Achieving the Budget Targets for Budget Years 2015 and 2016), 5776-2015, Sefer
--    HaChukim 2511 (30.11.2015) p. 244. Its s 28 substitutes paragraph (2) of "הסכום הבסיסי"
--    (150 / 188 / 140) and amends s 68(b) and (c) to their present wording; its s 29(a) reads,
--    on p. 247:
-- ext:[sh-5776-247] | תחילתם של סעיפים 1 ו–68 לחוק הביטוח הלאומי, כנוסחם בסימן זה, ביום י"ב באייר התשע"ה (1 במאי 2015) (בסעיף זה - היום הקובע)
--    Fetched 2026-10-06 as the raw bytes of an Internet Archive capture of the Knesset's PDF
--    (fs.knesset.gov.il answered a direct fetch with an HTML "Unavailable" page):
--      https://web.archive.org/web/20151217003808id_/http://fs.knesset.gov.il//20/law/20_lsr_316719.pdf
--      44 pp., sha256 6c99d23c7d2521bd8691d5cc7b62c43eca6d76fec27f8ee0d2958dfee9c50797
--    Re-fetched 2026-10-06 14:50 UTC from https://fs.knesset.gov.il/20/law/20_lsr_316719.pdf
--    through an Israeli-IP SOCKS proxy: the same 434,026 bytes, the same sha256.
--    The PDF's text layer stores each line in visual order. The quotation was rebuilt from
--    `pdftotext -raw` of page 31 by reversing each line's word order; its 19 Hebrew words were
--    checked by script to occur contiguously in that layer, and its digits and punctuation by
--    eye against the page rendered as an image (NOTES.md section 7).
--
-- So the deposited text answers days FROM 1 MAY 2015 (NOTES.md, assumption A1). Nothing in
-- the sources ends it; the figures, which change each 1 January, are bounded separately.
--
-- The day is taken as an explicit input rather than through `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` (NOTES.md,
-- assumption A2): for a monthly benefit the day asked about fixes at once the child's age, the
-- facts, and the text and figures in force, and one input keeps them from drifting apart.

§ `The period this encoding answers`

@ref Economic Efficiency Law 5776-2015 s 29(a) (Sefer HaChukim 2511 p. 247): ss 1 and 68 of the National Insurance Law, as worded by that Law, commence on 1 May 2015
GIVETH A DATE
`the day sections 1 and 68 took their present wording` MEANS YMD 2015 5 1

@ref National Insurance Law ss 65-68 (source lines 799-834): amendment tags end at תשע״ו־3
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the deposited text of sections 65 to 68 was in force on` `the day` MEANS
    `the day` AT LEAST `the day sections 1 and 68 took their present wording`

@ref Economic Efficiency Law 5776-2015 s 29(a); the text of ss 1 and 68 in force before 1 May 2015 is not in this row's sources
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`this model answers days from 1 May 2015, when sections 1 and 68 took their present wording; the text in force before then is not in its sources` MEANS
    REFUSE "this model answers days from 1 May 2015, when sections 1 and 68 took their present wording; the text in force before then is not in its sources"
